Assigning to __proto__ through a dynamic key sets the prototype.
-- script.js --
const k = "__proto__";
const o = {own: 1};
o[k] = {inherited: 2};
return [o.inherited, Object.keys(o), JSON.stringify(o)];
-- tools.json --
{}
-- divergence --
Assigning __proto__ through a dynamic key is outside the subset and raises ErrRuntimeUnsupported (hosts fall back when no effect has happened).
